        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Brierfield, Lancashire, England; Burnley Central; Colne\n- Organizations: Northern; Borough of Pendle\n- Systems: East Lancashire Line\n- Topics: Brierfield railway station; population\n\nFacts:\n- Brierfield is a small town and civil parish in the Borough of Pendle, Lancashire, England.\n- Brierfield had a population of 8,200, which reduced slightly to 8,193 at the 2011 Census.\n- Brierfield railway station serves the town of Brierfield in Lancashire, England.\n- Brierfield railway station is on the East Lancashire Line, 2+1/4 miles east of Burnley Central railway station toward the terminus at Colne.\n- Northern manages Brierfield railway station and provides all passenger train services there.",
